, "Incumbent Frank J. Mrvan (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Northwest Indiana's 1st District leans slightly Democratic, and incumbent Frank Mrvan is seeking re-election against Republican Barb Regnitz, who carries a Trump endorsement. Ten expert ratings split between Safe D and Likely D, and prediction markets put Mrvan's chances near 97 percent. With no public general-election polls, the picture rests on the district's modest Democratic lean and a national climate that favors Democrats this cycle.\n\nFundraising is nearly even: Mrvan has raised about $2.4 million, while Regnitz has matched that total and holds more cash on hand. Still, no major outside spending has targeted Mrvan, a sign both sides view the seat as secondary. Mrvan has been visible on local issues such as utility costs and labor lockouts. The race remains Likely Democratic, with Regnitz needing an unusually strong environment to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9569, "margin": 11.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9243, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9241, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9308, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9246, "margin": 10.6}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9079, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9227, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9457, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9206, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9443, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.938, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9373, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9482, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9254, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9274, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9315, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9183, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9321, "margin": 10.8}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9084, "ma